 "feasibility_issues": [
  "as_built (tilt 30, h 48): fp9_camera_wedge_bridge is in frame (35403 px)",
  "tilt0_h48 (tilt 0, h 48): 5% of the wall frog's camera-facing surface is cut off (5% lies outside the sensor image)",
  "tilt30_h30 (tilt 30, h 30): the lens point lies inside fp9_camera_wedge_bridge, so this height needs a different seat; with that part left out the view gives top disc 99%, disc frog 6.0 px/mm, wall frog 8.4 px/mm"
 ],
 "recommendation": "As built (tilt 30 deg, lens 48 mm above the disc) the camera sees 99% of the top disc inside the tube and nothing on the rotor blocks either frog (100% / 100% of their camera-facing triangles unblocked; 65% / 63% are seen first, the rest hidden by the frogs' own legs), at 6.8 px/mm on the disc frog and 9.8 px/mm on the wall frog, so the placement works for both frogs. The best configuration of the sweep is tilt30_h66 (tilt 30 deg, h 66 mm: top disc 99%, disc frog 65% at 7.9 px/mm, wall frog 64% at 10.9 px/mm), scored on coverage of both frogs and the disc plus resolution. Resolution is not the limit: every configuration clear of its mount gives at least 6.8 px/mm on both frogs at the full 2592 x 1944 sensor (the brief's floor is 2); the lens heights below the bridge top (30 mm) put the lens inside fp9_camera_wedge_bridge and would need a new seat; steeper tilts push the -X edge of the top disc out of the frame (as_built 99%, tilt0_h48 99%, tilt15_h48 99%, tilt30_h48 99%, tilt45_h48 99%, tilt30_h66 99%). tilt30_h66 only buys about 15% more resolution, so the as-built 30 deg / 48 mm placement works and can stay.",
 "fails": [],
 "seconds": 125.0
